# Database settings
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://root:password@localhost:5432/community?schema=public

# JWT secret token
JWT_SECRET=abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz1234567890

# S3 settings
# S3_BUCKET is PRIVATE and must stay private. It holds enrollment identity
# documents — birth certificates, social security cards and state IDs. Never
# make this bucket or any object in it publicly readable, and never relax its
# policy to make a website image load.
S3_REGION=us-east-1
S3_BUCKET=community
S3_ACCESS_KEY=minioadmin
S3_SECRET_KEY=minioadmin
S3_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:9000
S3_PROVIDER=minio

# Website Studio media library — images shown on the PUBLIC site (logo, hero
# portraits, illustrations). These live in a SEPARATE, public bucket, because
# they are served to every anonymous visitor while S3_BUCKET holds identity
# documents that must never be readable without a signed URL. One bucket
# cannot be both; putting site images in S3_BUCKET and then making it readable
# would expose every enrollment document in it.
#
# The API refuses to start if S3_PUBLIC_BUCKET equals S3_BUCKET.
#
# Leave both blank to run without the media library: uploads report "media
# storage is not configured" and the site serves the images that shipped in
# git (apps/web/src/content/media-slots.ts). Nothing else is affected.
#
# S3_PUBLIC_URL is the public base URL objects in that bucket are served from
# (a CDN domain, or e.g. http://localhost:9000/community-site-media for MinIO).
# Its host must also be allowed in apps/web/next.config.ts, which reads it.
S3_PUBLIC_BUCKET=
S3_PUBLIC_URL=